  "caption": "A British naval wireless pioneer once claimed his homemade radio could \u201ctune in\u201d to fairies.\n\nIn the 1920s he treated the sounds\u2014harps, bells, and voices\u2014as a signal problem, and built a formal society to collect reports like evidence.\n\nThe odd part is not the folklore, but the paperwork: modern Britain briefly tried to measure the unseen with letterheads, tests, and a census.\n\nThe story unfolds slide by slide.\n\n#TheBoldUnknown #TheUnknownExplained #Curiosity #ScienceAndSociety #StrangeButTrue #HistoricalMystery #HiddenHistory #Anomalies #FolkloreStudies #PatternRecognition",
